## CI #1644 + P1 corrective

CI #1644 exposed four assertion mismatches caused by the intentional Stage-5C copy changes, not production-state failures:

- two new button assertions were too whitespace-strict for multiline EJS output;
- one older Release-history test still expected `changes Studio only` instead of the new `changes Working only` language;
- one first-draft truthfulness test still expected `Nothing is live yet` instead of `No Website Release yet`.

Those regressions have been aligned with the new terminology.

Independent review also identified a real P1: a persisted verified public proof could have caused an interrupted `deploying` record to be summarized as **Public site is online and verified**. Corrected by:

- handling `deploying` before the stable verified branch;
- presenting **Public update is incomplete** with an explicit resume/recovery next step;
- restricting the verified human status to stable `healthy` / `rollback-available` states;
- adding a deterministic regression where stale verified endpoint evidence exists on an interrupted deployment and must not produce a verified human summary.

New exact candidate:

```text
HEAD = 8382ef791f68738266d5538d6dfa644b10881be9
```

Fresh qualification is running on this exact head.

## CI #1657 + P1 corrective

CI #1657 failed on one Stage-5C assertion that still expected the superseded phrase `Website Release online:` after the human-facing copy had moved to `Public site is serving:`.

The same exact-head audit also surfaced the remaining P1 in the active-Release summary: `activeRelease` was still labeled as currently serving even during interrupted recovery states.

Corrected both together:

- stable + publicly verified deployment: **Public site is serving**;
- `deploying` / `degraded` / `unreachable`: **Last confirmed deployed Website Release**;
- other confirmed server-only states: **Website Release confirmed on server**;
- regression now forbids `Public site is serving` during interrupted deployment recovery.

New exact candidate follows after both commits; fresh qualification will replace CI #1657.
